  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As pressure against which expansion is happening is constant, work done can be written as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1600</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>480</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br />As only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of heat is used in work done.<br />Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br />The rest goes in increase in internal energy, which is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of heat.<br />Change in internal energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4800</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4320</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>",
